      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Raymond buzzed with lumber mills, trains hauling freshly cut logs, and ships loading timber at its docks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofraymond.com/about-us/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic downtown Raymond is home to Willapa Paddle Adventures, where visitors paddle the Willapa River and learn about its rich history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.evergreencoastwa.com/cities-communities/raymond/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A collection of 200 sculptures around town depicts local wildlife and scenes, so realistic that passers‑by swear they’re real.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.evergreencoastwa.com/cities-communities/raymond/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Northwest Carriage Museum showcases stories from elegant carriages, sleighs, stagecoaches, and commercial wagons that once roamed the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.evergreencoastwa.com/cities-communities/raymond/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Raymond’s waterfront hosts the Willapa Harbor Chamber of Commerce and the Willapa Seaport Museum, preserving the town’s maritime heritage.",
